Complete AWS Architecture Project
In this project we will build a fully connected AWS environment from scratch using Terraform. The architecture consists of the following components:
Network Layer:

A VPC to define our private network boundary
A Subnet inside the VPC where our EC2 instance will live
An Internet Gateway (IGW) attached to the VPC to allow internet connectivity
A Route Table with a route pointing 0.0.0.0/0 to the IGW, associated to the subnet to allow traffic flow between the subnet and the internet

Security Layer:

A Security Group attached to the EC2 instance with an inbound (ingress) rule allowing SSH on port 22

Compute Layer:

An EC2 Instance placed inside the subnet, assigned a public IP address so it can be reached from the internet


The full dependency chain looks like this:
VPC
 ├── Subnet
 ├── Internet Gateway
 ├── Route Table (0.0.0.0/0 → IGW)
 │    └── Associated to Subnet
 ├── Security Group (allow SSH port 22)
 └── EC2 Instance
      ├── placed in Subnet
      ├── attached to Security Group
      └── assigned Public IP